[2026-03-14T19:37:09.762Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012hxTMVpqmVpD6oxjBsChFP","type":"tool_result","content":"   100→- **Action**: User types in the password field\n   101→- **Expected**: The input is masked (displayed as dots/bullets), the field type is \"password\".\n   102→\n   103→#### Test: Sign up form can be submitted via Enter key\n   104→- **Initial state**: User is on `/signup`, has entered valid name, email, and password\n   105→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the password field\n   106→- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Create account\".\n   107→\n   108→#### Test: Sign up redirects authenticated users\n   109→- **Initial state**: User is already authenticated (valid session token in localStorage)\n   110→- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n   111→- **Expected**: User is redirected to `/my-issues` instead of seeing the sign up form.\n   112→\n   113→## Navigation Sidebar\n   114→\n   115→**Components**: Sidebar, SidebarCollapse, KeyboardShortcuts\n   116→\n   117→### Sidebar\n   118→\n   119→#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace header\n   120→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   121→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays the workspace name at the top. The workspace name is clickable.\n   122→\n   123→#### Test: Sidebar workspace header navigates to home\n   124→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and viewing `/team/1/issues`\n   125→- **Action**: User clicks the workspace name in the sidebar header\n   126→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues` (home page).\n   127→\n   128→#### Test: Sidebar renders main navigation links\n   129→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   130→- **Expected**: The sidebar shows \"My Issues\" with a user-circle icon and \"Inbox\" with an inbox icon. Both are clickable navigation links.\n   131→\n   132→#### Test: Sidebar My Issues link navigates correctly\n   133→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`\n   134→- **Action**: User clicks \"My Issues\" in the sidebar\n   135→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`. The \"My Issues\" link appears selected/active with visual distinction (e.g., highlighted background).\n   136→\n   137→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox link navigates correctly\n   138→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   139→- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n   140→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The \"Inbox\" link appears selected/active.\n   141→\n   142→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox shows unread notification count badge\n   143→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications\n   144→- **Expected**: The \"Inbox\" link in the sidebar displays a badge showing \"3\". The badge is visually distinct (e.g., accent color background).\n   145→\n   146→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge updates when notifications are read\n   147→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, badge shows \"3\"\n   148→- **Action**: User navigates to `/inbox` and marks one notification as read\n   149→- **Expected**: The badge count updates to \"2\". If all notifications are read, the badge disappears.\n   150→\n   151→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge not shown when no unread notifications\n   152→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 0 unread notifications\n   153→- **Expected**: No badge is shown next to the \"Inbox\" link.\n   154→\n   155→#### Test: Sidebar renders team sections\n   156→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n   157→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Team Section\" with each team name as a collapsible section header. Under each team: \"Issues\" (list icon), \"Active Cycle\" (refresh-cw icon), \"Projects\" (folder icon), \"Views\" (layout icon).\n   158→\n   159→#### Test: Sidebar team section is collapsible\n   160→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n   161→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" team section header\n   162→- **Expected**: The team section collapses, hiding Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, and Views sub-links. Clicking again expands it back.\n   163→\n   164→#### Test: Sidebar team section collapse toggles multiple times\n   165→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n   166→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" header to collapse, then clicks it again to expand, then collapses it once more\n   167→- **Expected**: Each click toggles the section correctly. After three clicks the section is collapsed.\n   168→\n   169→#### Test: Sidebar team Issues link navigates to team issues page\n   170→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   171→- **Action**: User clicks \"Issues\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   172→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/issues`. The link appears selected/active.\n   173→\n   174→#### Test: Sidebar team Active Cycle link navigates to cycles page\n   175→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   176→- **Action**: User clicks \"Active Cycle\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   177→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Sidebar team Projects link navigates to team projects\n   180→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   181→- **Action**: User clicks \"Projects\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   182→- **Expected**: User is navigated to the projects page filtered by this team, or to `/projects` with the team filter applied.\n   183→\n   184→#### Test: Sidebar team Views link navigates to saved views\n   185→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   186→- **Action**: User clicks \"Views\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   187→- **Expected**: User is navigated to a views page for the team showing saved filtered views.\n   188→\n   189→#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace section links\n   190→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n   191→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n   192→\n   193→#### Test: Sidebar All Projects link navigates correctly\n   194→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   195→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Projects\" in the workspace section\n   196→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/projects`.\n   197→\n   198→#### Test: Sidebar All Teams link navigates correctly\n   199→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   200→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Teams\" in the workspace section\n   201→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/teams`.\n   202→\n   203→#### Test: Sidebar Members link navigates correctly\n   204→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   205→- **Action**: User clicks \"Members\" in the workspace section\n   206→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/members`.\n   207→\n   208→#### Test: Sidebar Labels link navigates correctly\n   209→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   210→- **Action**: User clicks \"Labels\" in the workspace section\n   211→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/labels`.\n   212→\n   213→#### Test: Sidebar Settings link navigates correctly\n   214→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   215→- **Action**: User clicks \"Settings\" in the workspace section\n   216→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings`.\n   217→\n   218→#### Test: Sidebar highlights current page link\n   219→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   220→- **Expected**: The \"My Issues\" link in the sidebar has an active/selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background, different text color). Other links do not have the active style.\n   221→\n   222→#### Test: Sidebar active highlight updates on navigation\n   223→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`, \"My Issues\" is highlighted\n   224→- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n   225→- **Expected**: \"Inbox\" becomes highlighted and \"My Issues\" loses its highlight.\n   226→\n   227→#### Test: Sidebar is present on all authenticated pages\n   228→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n   229→- **Action**: User navigates to `/my-issues`, then `/inbox`, then `/settings`\n   230→- **Expected**: The sidebar is visible and functional on all three pages with consistent layout and content.\n   231→\n   232→#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on login page\n   233→- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n   234→- **Action**: User navigates to `/login`\n   235→- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the login form is shown.\n   236→\n   237→#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on signup page\n   238→- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n   239→- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n   240→- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the signup form is shown.\n   241→\n   242→### SidebarCollapse\n   243→\n   244→#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle button is visible\n   245→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n   246→- **Expected**: A toggle button is visible on the sidebar (e.g., a chevron-left icon or hamburger icon) that can collapse the sidebar.\n   247→\n   248→#### Test: Sidebar collapses to icon-only mode\n   249→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is fully expanded showing labels and icons"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJzCzLNg8CQ19fUkzZhFgY","session_id":"6da3f93c-eebf-4489-9bbd-9b71bb41a908","uuid":"0f9650bf-b1df-43d2-b966-d23bd974a85e"}
