[2026-03-14T19:37:25.940Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JMLTftR56kQQc7QuzBj4mT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import type { Context } from '@netlify/functions';\n     2→import { getSql } from './db';\n     3→\n     4→export default async function handler(req: Request, _context: Context) {\n     5→  if (req.method !== 'PUT') {\n     6→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Method not allowed' }), {\n     7→      status: 405,\n     8→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n     9→    });\n    10→  }\n    11→\n    12→  try {\n    13→    const authHeader = req.headers.get('Authorization');\n    14→    if (!authHeader?.startsWith('Bearer ')) {\n    15→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Unauthorized' }), {\n    16→        status: 401,\n    17→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    18→      });\n    19→    }\n    20→\n    21→    const token = authHeader.slice(7);\n    22→    const sql = getSql();\n    23→\n    24→    const sessions = await sql`\n    25→      SELECT s.member_id FROM sessions s\n    26→      WHERE s.token = ${token} AND s.expires_at > NOW()\n    27→    `;\n    28→    const session = sessions[0];\n    29→    if (!session) {\n    30→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Unauthorized' }), {\n    31→        status: 401,\n    32→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    33→      });\n    34→    }\n    35→\n    36→    const { issueIds, status, priority, assigneeId, labelId } = await req.json();\n    37→\n    38→    if (!issueIds || !Array.isArray(issueIds) || issueIds.length === 0) {\n    39→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'issueIds array is required' }), {\n    40→        status: 400,\n    41→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    42→      });\n    43→    }\n    44→\n    45→    if (status) {\n    46→      const validStatuses = ['backlog', 'todo', 'in_progress', 'in_review', 'done', 'cancelled'];\n    47→      if (!validStatuses.includes(status)) {\n    48→        return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid status' }), {\n    49→          status: 400,\n    50→          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    51→        });\n    52→      }\n    53→      await sql`\n    54→        UPDATE issues SET status = ${status}, updated_at = NOW()\n    55→        WHERE id = ANY(${issueIds})\n    56→      `;\n    57→    }\n    58→\n    59→    if (priority) {\n    60→      const validPriorities = ['urgent', 'high', 'medium', 'low', 'none'];\n    61→      if (!validPriorities.includes(priority)) {\n    62→        return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid priority' }), {\n    63→          status: 400,\n    64→          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    65→        });\n    66→      }\n    67→      await sql`\n    68→        UPDATE issues SET priority = ${priority}, updated_at = NOW()\n    69→        WHERE id = ANY(${issueIds})\n    70→      `;\n    71→    }\n    72→\n    73→    if (assigneeId !== undefined) {\n    74→      const assignee = assigneeId || null;\n    75→      await sql`\n    76→        UPDATE issues SET assignee_id = ${assignee}, updated_at = NOW()\n    77→        WHERE id = ANY(${issueIds})\n    78→      `;\n    79→    }\n    80→\n    81→    if (labelId) {\n    82→      for (const issueId of issueIds) {\n    83→        const existing = await sql`\n    84→          SELECT 1 FROM issue_labels WHERE issue_id = ${issueId} AND label_id = ${labelId}\n    85→        `;\n    86→        if (existing.length === 0) {\n    87→          await sql`\n    88→            INSERT INTO issue_labels (issue_id, label_id) VALUES (${issueId}, ${labelId})\n    89→          `;\n    90→        }\n    91→      }\n    92→    }\n    93→\n    94→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true }), {\n    95→      status: 200,\n    96→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    97→    });\n    98→  } catch (err) {\n    99→    console.error('Bulk update issues error:', err);\n   100→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Internal server error' }), {\n   101→      status: 500,\n   102→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   103→    });\n   104→  }\n   105→}\n   106→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJzCzLNg8CQ19fUkzZhFgY","session_id":"6da3f93c-eebf-4489-9bbd-9b71bb41a908","uuid":"5e780b8d-132f-493b-86b0-c73a79870ee2"}
[2026-03-14T19:37:56.885Z] {"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a36f9bf6ea20ad1dc","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJzCzLNg8CQ19fUkzZhFgY","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"Explore Linear clone app structure","usage":{"total_tokens":84954,"tool_uses":56,"duration_ms":134352},"uuid":"489c7888-3bdc-4475-85f2-9f3a6069bf92","session_id":"6da3f93c-eebf-4489-9bbd-9b71bb41a908"}
[2026-03-14T19:37:56.886Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJzCzLNg8CQ19fUkzZhFgY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive exploration report:\n\n## Comprehensive LinearClone App Exploration Report\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Linear clone app codebase. Here's everything you need to know to build the IssueDetail page and its associated components:\n\n### PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/`\n\n**Key directories**:\n- `/src/components/` - Reusable React components (20+ components)\n- `/src/pages/` - Page components (Login, SignUp, MyIssues, Inbox, TeamIssues)\n- `/src/slices/` - Redux Toolkit slices (auth, issues, teamIssues, teams, workspace, labels, notifications, ui)\n- `/netlify/functions/` - Backend API endpoints\n\n**Existing components** (reference for patterns):\n- `IssueRow.tsx` - Displays individual issue rows with status/priority icons, labels, assignee avatar\n- `TeamIssuesList.tsx` - Lists team issues with grouping (status, priority, assignee, project, label, none)\n- `MyIssuesList.tsx` - Lists issues assigned to current user, grouped by status\n- `Sidebar.tsx` - Navigation sidebar with workspace, teams, and settings links\n- `CreateIssueForm.tsx` - Form for creating new issues with all fields\n- `FiltersToolbar.tsx`, `TeamFilters.tsx`, `GroupBySort.tsx` - Filtering and sorting\n- `NotificationList.tsx`, `NotificationRow.tsx` - Notification display\n\n### DATA MODEL & SLICES\n\n**Issue interface** (`issuesSlice.ts`):\n```typescript\ninterface Issue {\n  id: string;\n  title: string;\n  description: string;\n  status: string; // 'backlog', 'todo', 'in_progress', 'in_review', 'done', 'cancelled'\n  priority: string; // 'urgent', 'high', 'medium', 'low', 'none'\n  identifier: string; // e.g., \"ENG-42\"\n  number: number;\n  dueDate: string | null;\n  createdAt: string;\n  updatedAt: string;\n  teamId: string;\n  teamName: string;\n  assigneeId: string | null;\n  assigneeName: string | null;\n  assigneeEmail: string | null;\n  projectId: string | null;\n  projectName: string | null;\n  cycleId: string | null;\n  parentId: string | null; // For sub-issues\n  labels: IssueLabel[]; // Array of {id, name, color}\n}\n```\n\n**Redux store** (`store.ts`):\n```\nauth, ui, teams, workspace, notifications, issues, labels, teamIssues\n```\n\n**Available thunks**:\n- `fetchMyIssues()` - GET /api/my-issues\n- `createIssue(payload)` - POST /api/create-issue\n- `updateIssueStatus({issueId, status})` - PUT /api/update-issue-status\n- `fetchLabels()` - GET /api/labels\n- `fetchTeams()` - GET /api/teams\n- `fetchWorkspace()` - GET /api/workspace\n\n### BACKEND API ENDPOINTS\n\n**Netlify functions** in `/netlify/functions/`:\n\n1. **team-issues.ts** - GET `/api/team-issues?teamId={teamId}`\n   - Returns: `{issues, members, projects, cycles}`\n   - Query database for team's issues with full details + labels + related data\n\n2. **my-issues.ts** - GET `/api/my-issues`\n   - Returns: `{issues}`\n   - Issues assigned to current user with full details and labels\n\n3. **create-issue.ts** - POST `/api/create-issue`\n   - Body: `{teamId, title, description, status, priority, assigneeId, labelIds, projectId, cycleId, dueDate, parentId}`\n   - Creates issue, inserts labels, creates activity entry, creates notifications\n\n4. **update-issue-status.ts** - PUT `/api/update-issue-status`\n   - Body: `{issueId, status}`\n   - Updates issue status, timestamps\n\n5. **search-issues.ts** - GET `/api/search-issues?q={query}&teamId={teamId}`\n   - Returns: `{issues: [{id, title, identifier}]}`\n   - Search issues by title/identifier\n\n**Authentication**: All endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header. Token stored in localStorage as `session_token`.\n\n### STYLING & DESIGN\n\n**Dark mode theme** (defined as CSS variables):\n- `--color-bg`: `#0f1117` (main background)\n- `--color-bg-surface`: `#1a1d24` (surface/elevated)\n- `--color-border`: `#2a2d35` (borders)\n- `--color-accent`: `#5e6ad2` (primary purple-blue)\n- `--color-text-primary`: primary text\n- `--color-text-secondary`: secondary text\n- `--color-text-tertiary`: muted text\n\n**Status colors**:\n- backlog: gray\n- todo: gray\n- in_progress: yellow\n- in_review: blue\n- done: green\n- cancelled: red\n\n**Priority colors**:\n- urgent: red\n- high: orange\n- medium: yellow\n- low: blue\n- none: gray\n\n**Component styling patterns**:\n- Uses CSS modules (component.css files)\n- Flexbox for layouts\n- Smooth transitions (150ms ease)\n- Compact spacing (36px issue row height)\n- SVG icons from Feather icon set\n\n### ROUTING & NAVIGATION\n\nBased on the spec and sidebar code, routes include:\n- `/login` - Login page\n- `/signup` - Sign up page\n- `/my-issues` - My issues page\n- `/inbox` - Notifications page\n- `/team/:teamId/issues` - Team issues page\n- `/team/:teamId/cycles` - Active cycles page\n- `/team/:teamId/projects` - Team projects page\n- `/team/:teamId/views` - Saved views\n- `/issue/:issueId` - **Issue detail page (TO BUILD)**\n- `/projects` - All projects\n- `/settings/teams` - Teams management\n- `/settings/members` - Members management\n- `/settings/labels` - Labels management\n- `/settings` - Workspace settings\n\n### ISSUE DETAIL PAGE REQUIREMENTS\n\nFrom `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` (lines 935-1200+):\n\n**Page structure**: Two-panel layout\n- **Left panel** (~70% width): IssueHeader, IssueDescription, SubIssues, ActivityComments\n- **Right panel** (~30% width): IssueSidebar\n\n**Components to build**:\n\n1. **IssueHeader**\n   - Displays issue identifier (non-editable) + title (inline editable)\n   - Inline status selector with dropdown\n   - Save on blur or Enter, cancel on Escape\n   - Validate title not empty\n   - Create activity entries on changes\n\n2. **IssueDescription**\n   - Renders markdown content\n   - Placeholder \"Add a description...\" when empty\n   - Click to edit (rich markdown editor)\n   - Save on blur, cancel on Escape\n   - Create activity entries on changes\n\n3. **SubIssues**\n   - List child issues with status/priority icons\n   - \"No sub-issues\" message when empty\n   - \"Add sub-issue\" button opens create modal with parent pre-filled\n   - Sub-issue rows clickable to navigate to detail page\n\n4. **ActivityComments**\n   - Tab toggle between \"Activity\" and \"Comments\"\n   - Activity: chronological entries showing changes (status, assignee, priority, etc.) with actor avatar, name, timestamp\n   - Comments: user comments with avatar, name, relative timestamp, content\n   - Comment input box at bottom with \"Comment\" button\n   - Button disabled when empty, enabled with text\n   - Submit on button click or Enter/Cmd+Enter\n   - Clear input after submit\n   - Create activity/notification entries on new comments\n\n5. **IssueSidebar**\n   - Status dropdown (same as header, triggers activity/notifications)\n   - Priority dropdown (urgent/high/medium/low/none)\n   - Assignee selector (searchable, shows avatar)\n   - Labels multi-select (colored badges)\n   - Project selector (searchable)\n   - Cycle selector (dropdown)\n   - Due date picker\n   - Created timestamp (read-only)\n   - Updated timestamp (read-only)\n\n**Data needed**:\n- Need new slice to manage issue detail state (currentIssue, activity, comments, subIssues)\n- Need async thunks to:\n  - Fetch single issue by ID with all details\n  - Fetch activity history for issue\n  - Fetch comments for issue\n  - Fetch sub-issues\n  - Update issue properties (title, description, priority, assignee, labels, project, cycle, dueDate)\n  - Create comments\n  - Create activity entries\n\n### EXISTING PATTERNS TO FOLLOW\n\n**Component patterns**:\n- Use React hooks (useState, useEffect, useCallback, useRef, useMemo)\n- Use Redux selectors with `useSelector`\n- Use `useDispatch` with typed `AppDispatch`\n- Dropdown handling: useRef + useEffect for outside-click detection\n- Icon components for status/priority (reuse from IssueRow.tsx: `StatusIcon`, `PriorityIcon`)\n- Avatar helper: `getInitials()` function\n\n**State management patterns**:\n- Create async thunks with error handling\n- Use `rejectWithValue` for error messages\n- Store loading/error states\n- Use `extraReducers` for async case handling\n\n**CSS patterns**:\n- Use CSS variables for colors\n- Flexbox for layout\n- Smooth transitions (150ms ease)\n- Data-testid attributes for all interactive elements\n- Responsive design with media queries\n\n**Networking**:\n- All requests need `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header\n- Use `getState` in thunks to get token from auth slice\n- Handle 401 responses (unauthorized)\n- Return proper HTTP status codes\n\n### AVAILABLE HELPER FUNCTIONS & EXPORTS\n\nFrom IssueRow.tsx:\n- `StatusIcon` component (status, color props)\n- `PriorityIcon` component (priority prop)\n- `STATUS_CONFIG` - maps status → {label, color}\n- `PRIORITY_CONFIG` - maps priority → {label, color}\n- `STATUS_ORDER` - correct ordering of statuses\n- `getInitials(name)` - converts name to initials\n\n### TESTING REQUIREMENTS\n\nFrom `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`:\n- 60+ test cases for Issue Detail page (lines 935+)\n- Tests cover: rendering, inline editing, status/priority changes, sub-issues, activity/comments, sidebar\n- Each test has: Initial state, Action(s), Expected behavior\n- Use data-testid attributes for all elements\n\n### FILE LOCATIONS\n\n**Key files to reference**:\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/issuesSlice.ts` - Issue types and fetch thunks\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueRow.tsx` - Status/Priority icons and configs\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/TeamIssues.tsx` - Page structure pattern\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.tsx` - Form patterns, dropdown handling\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/TeamIssuesList.tsx` - List rendering patterns\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/team-issues.ts` - Backend query patterns\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` - Complete test specifications\n\n---\n\nYou now have everything needed to build the IssueDetail page and its five components. The codebase is well-structured with clear patterns for Redux state management, async API calls, form handling, and styling. All the infrastructure is in place - you just need to implement the new components and backend functions to fetch/update individual issue details, activity logs, and comments."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a36f9bf6ea20ad1dc (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 87680\ntool_uses: 56\nduration_ms: 134355</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6da3f93c-eebf-4489-9bbd-9b71bb41a908","uuid":"4fa1a69d-0ea7-4d41-b08e-49fd3aa1b805","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Linear clone app thoroughly. I need to understand:\n\n1. Read apps/linear-clone/AppSpec.md (or similar spec file)\n2. Read apps/linear-clone/AppRevisions.md if it exists\n3. Read apps/AppStyle.md and apps/linear-clone/AppStyle.md if they exist\n4. Read docs/tests.md for test requirements\n5. List all files in apps/linear-clone/src/ recursively to understand existing components and pages\n6. Read the existing store.ts, App.tsx, main.tsx, and index.css\n7. Read existing slices (especially issues slice)\n8. Read existing components and pages to understand patterns used\n9. Read the database schema (scripts/schema.ts)\n10. Read existing netlify functions related to issues\n11. Check apps/shared/ for reusable components\n\nBe very thorough - read all relevant files completely. I need to build IssueHeader, IssueDescription, SubIssues, ActivityComments, IssueSidebar components and an IssueDetail page.","agentId":"a36f9bf6ea20ad1dc","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive exploration report:\n\n## Comprehensive LinearClone App Exploration Report\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Linear clone app codebase. Here's everything you need to know to build the IssueDetail page and its associated components:\n\n### PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/`\n\n**Key directories**:\n- `/src/components/` - Reusable React components (20+ components)\n- `/src/pages/` - Page components (Login, SignUp, MyIssues, Inbox, TeamIssues)\n- `/src/slices/` - Redux Toolkit slices (auth, issues, teamIssues, teams, workspace, labels, notifications, ui)\n- `/netlify/functions/` - Backend API endpoints\n\n**Existing components** (reference for patterns):\n- `IssueRow.tsx` - Displays individual issue rows with status/priority icons, labels, assignee avatar\n- `TeamIssuesList.tsx` - Lists team issues with grouping (status, priority, assignee, project, label, none)\n- `MyIssuesList.tsx` - Lists issues assigned to current user, grouped by status\n- `Sidebar.tsx` - Navigation sidebar with workspace, teams, and settings links\n- `CreateIssueForm.tsx` - Form for creating new issues with all fields\n- `FiltersToolbar.tsx`, `TeamFilters.tsx`, `GroupBySort.tsx` - Filtering and sorting\n- `NotificationList.tsx`, `NotificationRow.tsx` - Notification display\n\n### DATA MODEL & SLICES\n\n**Issue interface** (`issuesSlice.ts`):\n```typescript\ninterface Issue {\n  id: string;\n  title: string;\n  description: string;\n  status: string; // 'backlog', 'todo', 'in_progress', 'in_review', 'done', 'cancelled'\n  priority: string; // 'urgent', 'high', 'medium', 'low', 'none'\n  identifier: string; // e.g., \"ENG-42\"\n  number: number;\n  dueDate: string | null;\n  createdAt: string;\n  updatedAt: string;\n  teamId: string;\n  teamName: string;\n  assigneeId: string | null;\n  assigneeName: string | null;\n  assigneeEmail: string | null;\n  projectId: string | null;\n  projectName: string | null;\n  cycleId: string | null;\n  parentId: string | null; // For sub-issues\n  labels: IssueLabel[]; // Array of {id, name, color}\n}\n```\n\n**Redux store** (`store.ts`):\n```\nauth, ui, teams, workspace, notifications, issues, labels, teamIssues\n```\n\n**Available thunks**:\n- `fetchMyIssues()` - GET /api/my-issues\n- `createIssue(payload)` - POST /api/create-issue\n- `updateIssueStatus({issueId, status})` - PUT /api/update-issue-status\n- `fetchLabels()` - GET /api/labels\n- `fetchTeams()` - GET /api/teams\n- `fetchWorkspace()` - GET /api/workspace\n\n### BACKEND API ENDPOINTS\n\n**Netlify functions** in `/netlify/functions/`:\n\n1. **team-issues.ts** - GET `/api/team-issues?teamId={teamId}`\n   - Returns: `{issues, members, projects, cycles}`\n   - Query database for team's issues with full details + labels + related data\n\n2. **my-issues.ts** - GET `/api/my-issues`\n   - Returns: `{issues}`\n   - Issues assigned to current user with full details and labels\n\n3. **create-issue.ts** - POST `/api/create-issue`\n   - Body: `{teamId, title, description, status, priority, assigneeId, labelIds, projectId, cycleId, dueDate, parentId}`\n   - Creates issue, inserts labels, creates activity entry, creates notifications\n\n4. **update-issue-status.ts** - PUT `/api/update-issue-status`\n   - Body: `{issueId, status}`\n   - Updates issue status, timestamps\n\n5. **search-issues.ts** - GET `/api/search-issues?q={query}&teamId={teamId}`\n   - Returns: `{issues: [{id, title, identifier}]}`\n   - Search issues by title/identifier\n\n**Authentication**: All endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header. Token stored in localStorage as `session_token`.\n\n### STYLING & DESIGN\n\n**Dark mode theme** (defined as CSS variables):\n- `--color-bg`: `#0f1117` (main background)\n- `--color-bg-surface`: `#1a1d24` (surface/elevated)\n- `--color-border`: `#2a2d35` (borders)\n- `--color-accent`: `#5e6ad2` (primary purple-blue)\n- `--color-text-primary`: primary text\n- `--color-text-secondary`: secondary text\n- `--color-text-tertiary`: muted text\n\n**Status colors**:\n- backlog: gray\n- todo: gray\n- in_progress: yellow\n- in_review: blue\n- done: green\n- cancelled: red\n\n**Priority colors**:\n- urgent: red\n- high: orange\n- medium: yellow\n- low: blue\n- none: gray\n\n**Component styling patterns**:\n- Uses CSS modules (component.css files)\n- Flexbox for layouts\n- Smooth transitions (150ms ease)\n- Compact spacing (36px issue row height)\n- SVG icons from Feather icon set\n\n### ROUTING & NAVIGATION\n\nBased on the spec and sidebar code, routes include:\n- `/login` - Login page\n- `/signup` - Sign up page\n- `/my-issues` - My issues page\n- `/inbox` - Notifications page\n- `/team/:teamId/issues` - Team issues page\n- `/team/:teamId/cycles` - Active cycles page\n- `/team/:teamId/projects` - Team projects page\n- `/team/:teamId/views` - Saved views\n- `/issue/:issueId` - **Issue detail page (TO BUILD)**\n- `/projects` - All projects\n- `/settings/teams` - Teams management\n- `/settings/members` - Members management\n- `/settings/labels` - Labels management\n- `/settings` - Workspace settings\n\n### ISSUE DETAIL PAGE REQUIREMENTS\n\nFrom `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` (lines 935-1200+):\n\n**Page structure**: Two-panel layout\n- **Left panel** (~70% width): IssueHeader, IssueDescription, SubIssues, ActivityComments\n- **Right panel** (~30% width): IssueSidebar\n\n**Components to build**:\n\n1. **IssueHeader**\n   - Displays issue identifier (non-editable) + title (inline editable)\n   - Inline status selector with dropdown\n   - Save on blur or Enter, cancel on Escape\n   - Validate title not empty\n   - Create activity entries on changes\n\n2. **IssueDescription**\n   - Renders markdown content\n   - Placeholder \"Add a description...\" when empty\n   - Click to edit (rich markdown editor)\n   - Save on blur, cancel on Escape\n   - Create activity entries on changes\n\n3. **SubIssues**\n   - List child issues with status/priority icons\n   - \"No sub-issues\" message when empty\n   - \"Add sub-issue\" button opens create modal with parent pre-filled\n   - Sub-issue rows clickable to navigate to detail page\n\n4. **ActivityComments**\n   - Tab toggle between \"Activity\" and \"Comments\"\n   - Activity: chronological entries showing changes (status, assignee, priority, etc.) with actor avatar, name, timestamp\n   - Comments: user comments with avatar, name, relative timestamp, content\n   - Comment input box at bottom with \"Comment\" button\n   - Button disabled when empty, enabled with text\n   - Submit on button click or Enter/Cmd+Enter\n   - Clear input after submit\n   - Create activity/notification entries on new comments\n\n5. **IssueSidebar**\n   - Status dropdown (same as header, triggers activity/notifications)\n   - Priority dropdown (urgent/high/medium/low/none)\n   - Assignee selector (searchable, shows avatar)\n   - Labels multi-select (colored badges)\n   - Project selector (searchable)\n   - Cycle selector (dropdown)\n   - Due date picker\n   - Created timestamp (read-only)\n   - Updated timestamp (read-only)\n\n**Data needed**:\n- Need new slice to manage issue detail state (currentIssue, activity, comments, subIssues)\n- Need async thunks to:\n  - Fetch single issue by ID with all details\n  - Fetch activity history for issue\n  - Fetch comments for issue\n  - Fetch sub-issues\n  - Update issue properties (title, description, priority, assignee, labels, project, cycle, dueDate)\n  - Create comments\n  - Create activity entries\n\n### EXISTING PATTERNS TO FOLLOW\n\n**Component patterns**:\n- Use React hooks (useState, useEffect, useCallback, useRef, useMemo)\n- Use Redux selectors with `useSelector`\n- Use `useDispatch` with typed `AppDispatch`\n- Dropdown handling: useRef + useEffect for outside-click detection\n- Icon components for status/priority (reuse from IssueRow.tsx: `StatusIcon`, `PriorityIcon`)\n- Avatar helper: `getInitials()` function\n\n**State management patterns**:\n- Create async thunks with error handling\n- Use `rejectWithValue` for error messages\n- Store loading/error states\n- Use `extraReducers` for async case handling\n\n**CSS patterns**:\n- Use CSS variables for colors\n- Flexbox for layout\n- Smooth transitions (150ms ease)\n- Data-testid attributes for all interactive elements\n- Responsive design with media queries\n\n**Networking**:\n- All requests need `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header\n- Use `getState` in thunks to get token from auth slice\n- Handle 401 responses (unauthorized)\n- Return proper HTTP status codes\n\n### AVAILABLE HELPER FUNCTIONS & EXPORTS\n\nFrom IssueRow.tsx:\n- `StatusIcon` component (status, color props)\n- `PriorityIcon` component (priority prop)\n- `STATUS_CONFIG` - maps status → {label, color}\n- `PRIORITY_CONFIG` - maps priority → {label, color}\n- `STATUS_ORDER` - correct ordering of statuses\n- `getInitials(name)` - converts name to initials\n\n### TESTING REQUIREMENTS\n\nFrom `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`:\n- 60+ test cases for Issue Detail page (lines 935+)\n- Tests cover: rendering, inline editing, status/priority changes, sub-issues, activity/comments, sidebar\n- Each test has: Initial state, Action(s), Expected behavior\n- Use data-testid attributes for all elements\n\n### FILE LOCATIONS\n\n**Key files to reference**:\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/issuesSlice.ts` - Issue types and fetch thunks\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueRow.tsx` - Status/Priority icons and configs\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/TeamIssues.tsx` - Page structure pattern\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.tsx` - Form patterns, dropdown handling\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/TeamIssuesList.tsx` - List rendering patterns\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/team-issues.ts` - Backend query patterns\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` - Complete test specifications\n\n---\n\nYou now have everything needed to build the IssueDetail page and its five components. The codebase is well-structured with clear patterns for Redux state 